{
  "id": "fluency-l1-two-brackets",
  "course": "quadratics",
  "lesson": "l1-two-brackets",
  "title": "Fluency: multiplying two brackets",
  "n": 20,
  "pass": 0.9,
  "minutes": 10,
  "families": [
    {
      "id": "expand-monic",
      "weight": 2,
      "skill": "expand two brackets",
      "vars": {
        "a": { "int": [-9, 9], "not": [0] },
        "b": { "int": [-9, 9], "not": [0] },
        "v": { "pick": ["x", "y", "t", "r"] }
      },
      "let": { "s": "a + b", "p": "a*b" },
      "where": ["a != b", "s != 0", "p != s"],
      "prompt": "Expand and simplify $({v}{a:+})({v}{b:+})$.",
      "widget": { "kind": "expression", "answer": "{poly(v; 1, s, p)}", "form": "expanded" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "firsts-lasts", "tex": "{poly(v; 1, 0, p)}", "line": "You multiplied the firsts and the lasts and skipped the two middle terms." },
        { "id": "swapped", "tex": "{poly(v; 1, p, s)}", "line": "You multiplied ${a}$ and ${b}$ for the middle term and added them for the last: the middle adds, the last multiplies." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "The middle term is ${a} + {b:()} = {s}$, so it is ${s:c}{v}$.",
        "The last term is ${a} \\times {b:()} = {p}$.",
        "So $({v}{a:+})({v}{b:+}) = {poly(v; 1, s, p)}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "expand-coefficient",
      "weight": 2,
      "skill": "expand two brackets with a coefficient",
      "vars": {
        "p": { "int": [1, 3] },
        "q": { "int": [-7, 7], "not": [0] },
        "r": { "int": [1, 3] },
        "s": { "int": [-7, 7], "not": [0] },
        "v": { "pick": ["x", "y", "t"] }
      },
      "let": { "lead": "p*r", "m1": "p*s", "m2": "q*r", "mid": "p*s + q*r", "last": "q*s" },
      "where": ["p*r > 1", "gcd(p, abs(q)) == 1", "gcd(r, abs(s)) == 1", "p != r or q != s", "mid != 0", "q + s != 0", "mid != q + s"],
      "prompt": "Expand and simplify $({p:c}{v}{q:+})({r:c}{v}{s:+})$.",
      "widget": { "kind": "expression", "answer": "{poly(v; lead, mid, last)}", "form": "expanded" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "firsts-lasts", "tex": "{poly(v; lead, 0, last)}", "line": "You multiplied the firsts and the lasts and skipped the two middle terms." },
        { "id": "added-numbers", "tex": "{poly(v; lead, q + s, last)}", "line": "You added ${q}$ and ${s}$ for the middle term, but each number is multiplied by the other bracket's ${v}$ term first." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "The first terms give ${p:c}{v} \\times {r:c}{v} = {lead:c}{v}^2$ and the last terms give ${q} \\times {s:()} = {last}$.",
        "The middle terms are ${poly(v; m1, 0)}$ and ${poly(v; m2, 0)}$, which collect to ${poly(v; mid, 0)}$.",
        "So the expansion is ${poly(v; lead, mid, last)}$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "expand-square",
      "weight": 1,
      "skill": "expand a squared bracket",
      "vars": {
        "a": { "int": [-12, 12], "not": [0] },
        "v": { "pick": ["x", "y", "t", "r"] }
      },
      "let": { "d": "2*a", "sq": "a^2" },
      "prompt": "Expand $({v}{a:+})^2$.",
      "widget": { "kind": "expression", "answer": "{poly(v; 1, d, sq)}", "form": "expanded" },
      "wrong": [
        { "id": "squares-only", "tex": "{poly(v; 1, 0, sq)}", "line": "You squared each term and lost the two middle strips." },
        { "id": "one-strip", "tex": "{poly(v; 1, a, sq)}", "line": "You counted one middle strip, but there are two of ${a:c}{v}$." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        "$({v}{a:+})^2 = ({v}{a:+})({v}{a:+})$.",
        "There are two middle strips of ${a:c}{v}$, which make ${d:c}{v}$, and the corner is ${a:()}^2 = {sq}$.",
        "So $({v}{a:+})^2 = {poly(v; 1, d, sq)}$."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
